            <div xml:id="d755">

                <pb facs="0931" n="829" xml:id="pg829"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4832/41–42.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador
                        Dudley.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 94.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No 210 of the 29th ultimo, inclosing copy of the note by which you expressed to
                    the foreign office on the same day this Government’s appreciation of Brazil’s
                    good offices in taking charge of American interests in Venezuela.</p>
                <p>Your note is approved.</p>
                <p>With renewed expressions of appreciation of Brazilian good offices and good
                    will,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
